L140: **Figure S1.** The all-out cycling performance was not notably affected by three weeks of SIT in either the
L141: vitamin or the placebo group. (a) Mean power output during each of the six bouts of 30 s all-out cycling
L142: in the untrained (first SIT session) and trained (last SIT session) states of participants receiving vitamins
L143: (n = 4) or placebo (n = 4). (b) Mean power during all six cycling bouts in the untrained (U) and trained
L144: (T) states. Peak power (c) and mean power (d) during the first cycling bout in the untrained and trained
L145: states. Data from each individual (●,○) and mean data (▲,Δ); n = 4 in each group. Two-way repeated
L146: measures ANOVA revealed no training effect or difference between the vitamin and the placebo groups
L147: for any of the measured parameters. (e) Mean blood lactate before (Pre) and 5 and 60 min SIT sessions
L148: performed in the untrained and trained states by subjects receiving vitamins (n = 5) or placebo (untrained
L149: state, n = 5; trained state, n = 3). Data are presented as mean ± SD; vitamin group (black bars and symbols);
L150: placebo group (white bars and symbols). Two-way repeated measures ANOVA showed no difference
L151: between the vitamin and the placebo groups at any time point.
L152: **Figure S2.** Gene expression of inflammatory mediators in the untrained state (UT, i.e. before the first SIT
L153: session) and the trained state (T; i.e. before the last SIT session). Data from vitamin-treated (●) and
L154: placebo-treated (○) individuals. mRNA expressions presented as 2 [-ΔCt], where ∆Ct = Ct[Target] Ct[Housekeeping]. Two-way repeated measures ANOVA for each revealed a significantly higher (*, _P_ <
L155: 0.05) mRNA expression of IL-1β in the placebo than in the vitamin group; no other differences were
L156: detected between the two groups or between the untrained and trained states within each group.
L157: **Figure S3.** Gene expression of ROS-related proteins in the untrained state (UT, i.e. before the first SIT
L158: session) and the trained state (T; i.e. before the last SIT session). Data from vitamin-treated (●) and
L159: placebo-treated (○) individuals. mRNA expressions presented as 2 [-ΔCt], where ∆Ct = Ct[Target] Ct[Housekeeping]. Two-way repeated measures ANOVA for each gene revealed a significantly training
L160: effect of NOX2 both in the vitamin and placebo groups (#, _P_ < 0.05) and higher mRNA expression of
L161: SOD1 in the placebo than in the vitamin group both in untrained (**, _P_ < 0.01) and trained (*, _P_ < 0.05)
L162: states; no other differences were detected between the two groups or between the untrained and trained
L163: states within each group.
L164: **Figure S4.** Gene expression of RyR1-C and -N in the untrained state (UT, i.e. before the first SIT session)
L165: and the trained state (T; i.e. before the last SIT session). Data from vitamin-treated (●) and placebo
L166: treated (○) individuals. mRNA expressions presented as 2 [-ΔCt], where ∆Ct = Ct[Target] Ct[Housekeeping]. Two-way repeated measures ANOVA for each gene revealed a significantly negative
L167: training effect of both RyR1-C and -N both in the vitamin group (#, _P_ < 0.05; ## _P_ < 0.01); no other
L168: differences were detected between the two groups or between the untrained and trained states within
L169: each group.
L170: **Figure S5.** Gene expression of SR Ca [2+] -handling proteins (other than RyR1) in the untrained state (UT,
L171: i.e. before the first SIT session) and the trained state (T; i.e. before the last SIT session). Data from vitamin
L172: treated (●) and placebo-treated (○) individuals. mRNA expressions presented as 2 [-ΔCt], where ∆Ct =
L173: Ct[Target] - Ct[Housekeeping]. Two-way repeated measures ANOVA for each gene revealed a
L174: significantly negative training effect of DHPR in the vitamin group (## _P_ < 0.01) and higher mRNA
L175: expression of CSQ1 in the vitamin than in the placebo group both in the untrained (**, _P_ < 0.01) and
L176: trained (*, _P_ < 0.05) states; no other differences were detected between the two groups or between the
L177: untrained and trained states within each group.
L178: **Figure S6.** Gene expression of mitochondria-related proteins (other than RyR1) in the untrained state
L179: (UT, i.e. before the first SIT session) and the trained state (T; i.e. before the last SIT session). Data from
L180: vitamin-treated (●) and placebo-treated (○) individuals. mRNA expressions presented as 2 [-ΔCt], where
L181: ∆Ct = Ct[Target] - Ct[Housekeeping]. Two-way repeated measures ANOVA for each gene revealed a
L182: significantly negative training effect of MFN2 in the vitamin group (# _P_ < 0.05) and higher mRNA
L183: expression of MUL1 in the placebo than in the vitamin group both in the untrained (*, _P_ < 0.05) and
L184: trained (**, _P_ < 0.01) states; no other differences were detected between the two groups or between the
L185: untrained and trained states within each group.
